import{_ as t,o as i,c as n,a2 as o}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 365 | Dou Continent · Soul-Beast Extinction Crisis: The Ecological Disaster of Predatory Cultivation","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 365 | Dou Continent · Soul-Beast Extinction Crisis: The Ecological Disaster of Predatory Cultivation","no":365,"module":2,"tags":["Dou Continent","Soul-Beast Extinction","Ecological Disaster","Predatory Cultivation","Myriad Races"],"related":["05-Myriad-Ranks-Together-Advance Basic Program","46-Environmental Protection Law","50-Myriad-Ranks Genealogy Overview"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0365_模块2-斗罗-魂兽灭绝危机-掠夺式修炼的生态灾难.md","filePath":"en/0365_模块2-斗罗-魂兽灭绝危机-掠夺式修炼的生态灾难.md"}'),a={name:"en/0365_模块2-斗罗-魂兽灭绝危机-掠夺式修炼的生态灾难.md"};function s(r,e,l,u,c,h){return i(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<h1 id="entry-365-dou-continent-·-soul-beast-extinction-crisis-the-ecological-disaster-of-predatory-cultivation" tabindex="-1">Entry 365 | Dou Continent · Soul-Beast Extinction Crisis: The Ecological Disaster of Predatory Cultivation <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-365-dou-continent-·-soul-beast-extinction-crisis-the-ecological-disaster-of-predatory-cultivation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 365 | Dou Continent · Soul-Beast Extinction Crisis: The Ecological Disaster of Predatory Cultivation&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Dou Continent System Decomposition (Entry 6) | Benchmark base: Documents 05, 46, 50</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-when-an-entire-species-is-treated-as-renewable-resource" tabindex="-1">Introduction: When an entire species is treated as &quot;renewable resource&quot; <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-when-an-entire-species-is-treated-as-renewable-resource" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: When an entire species is treated as &quot;renewable resource&quot;&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Myriad Ranks republican axiom requires all beings to have equal evolution qualification. Dou Continent&#39;s soul beasts are the most thoroughly defined race among Myriad Ranks — they are not neighbors, not kin, but &quot;walking soul rings.&quot; As cultivator numbers grow and soul-ring demand inflates, the most direct consequence is soul-beast population collapse. This entry, taking the law-first axiom as core, argues this ecological disaster is no accident, but the inevitable product of predatory cultivation. Protagonist uniqueness dependency: <strong>high (gift-style leaning oligarchic)</strong>. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s judging base has been upgraded to the six top-level axioms.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>High-tier populations collapse first</strong>: rarer ten-thousand-year and hundred-thousand-year soul beasts are geniuses&#39; prime hunt targets; the most precious gene banks disappear first</li><li><strong>Food-chain rupture</strong>: soul beasts have ecological functions in the forest food chain; their sharp decline desertifies entire hunting grounds</li><li><strong>Irreversible loss</strong>: a hundred-thousand-year soul-beast species going extinct loses the Origin diversity the plane accumulated over millennia</li></ul><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Resource curve inversion</strong>: more cultivators → fewer soul beasts → harder for latecomers to break through; civilization ceiling declines with population growth</li><li><strong>Hunting ground desertification</strong>: hunting grounds like the Star Dou Great Forest degrade from &quot;rich&quot; to &quot;exhausted&quot;; the young generation has no rings to hunt</li><li><strong>Late patches to extend life</strong>: relying on &quot;spirit souls&quot; and &quot;farmed soul beasts&quot; to extend life is essentially admitting the hunting road cannot continue</li></ol><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Selective sympathy</strong>: Tang San has warmth toward human-form soul beasts like Xiao Wu, but continues hunting the uncountable non-human-form soul beasts — sympathy only for &quot;human-like,&quot; not for &quot;merely beasts&quot;</li><li><strong>Scale-insensitivity</strong>: at the individual level he kills only one each time, but accumulated, genius groups are precisely the main force of soul-beast extinction</li><li><strong>No ecological rescue</strong>: after becoming a god, he holds divine power enough to reverse the ecology, yet pushes no soul-beast protection institution</li></ul><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Dou Hunting Ecology</th><th>Anchor Symbiosis Alternative</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Soul beast = consumable</td><td>Soul beasts filed into Myriad-Ranks genealogy, protected by equal evolution qualification</td></tr><tr><td>High-tier extinct first</td><td>Alaya whole-network population monitoring; red-line species trigger intervention</td></tr><tr><td>Hunting ground desertified</td><td>Environmental Protection Law + life-circulation system; hunting grounds perpetual</td></tr><tr><td>Human-form exception</td><td>Myriad Ranks republicanism does not distribute rights by &quot;human-like&quot;</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The alternative&#39;s crux: Path D · human-engineered Dao-Law soul rings eliminate the &quot;must kill soul beasts&quot; need at the source; the ecological disaster is institutionally dismantled in advance.</p><p>What cuts off this ecological disaster at the source is the combination of Path D · human-engineered Dao-Law soul rings and Alaya population monitoring: the former makes humans no longer need to hunt soul beasts; the latter gives remnant soul-beast populations institutional protection. Lin Hao-style reconstructors will not continue selective blindness toward non-human-form soul beasts, but bring the whole soul-beast race into Myriad Ranks republicanism — it need not human-form itself to be treated as a life, not &quot;a ring a few years short of being stripped.&quot;</p><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Modeling</strong>: replicate soul-beast population—hunt demand dynamics</li><li><strong>Variables</strong>: Group A unprotected hunting; Group B inject Path D + Alaya population monitoring</li><li><strong>Observation</strong>: ten-thousand-year soul-beast population survivors, species-extinction rate</li><li><strong>Review</strong>: output &quot;Soul-Beast Extinction Timepoint Prediction and Institutional Hedging Benefit&quot;</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Setting self-consistency: low</strong>. The Star Dou Great Forest goes from vast hunting ground to late &quot;almost gone&quot;; order of magnitude contradicts early</li><li><strong>Retcon-ending risk: high</strong>. To supply rings for the protagonist, soul-beast resources fluctuate, entirely serving plot</li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness dependency: high</strong></li></ul><p>Soul-beast extinction is not an apocalyptic episode, but a settlement table written into the setting. High-tier soul beasts extinct first; latecomers can only hunt low-tier; the overall ceiling moves down with stock. The Star Dou Great Forest from rich to exhausted is precisely the negative-sum loop&#39;s直观 curve — the more successful the hunt, the more barren the hunting ground.</p><p>Soul-beast extinction also has an overlooked cascading consequence: ecological-niche vacuum. High-tier soul beasts play key roles in the forest food chain and plane energy loop; after their sharp decline, low-tier soul beasts and plant spirits lose evolutionary checks; the whole hunting ground degenerates from ecological prosperity to desert. This secondary disaster is often harder to recover from than direct hunting — hunting can stop, but once ecology loses balance, it takes a long time to self-heal, and the Dou world never gave that time.</p><p>The ecological disaster also has an intergenerational-justice dimension. The current generation of human cultivators enjoys the dividends of hunting soul beasts, yet leaves the &quot;no beasts to hunt&quot; desert to descendants. This is not a fair intergenerational contract, but an overdraft. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s life-circulation system precisely ensures cultivation does not crowd out descendants&#39; living space. The reason Path D is repeatedly emphasized is not only its zero killing, but that it makes each generation&#39;s cultivation incremental accumulation rather than stock overdraft — descendants inherit not a desert, but a world thicker than their parents&#39;.</p><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: high-tier soul-beast gene bank irreversibly lost</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: an entire race defined as consumables</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo excludes Myriad Ranks but at least does not hunt them; Tang San&#39;s system directly consumes one of Myriad Ranks</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: soul beasts are the race most deserving of rescue under the 99% Myriad-Ranks full-coverage claim</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: a system that actively exterminates neighbor races cannot coexist with multiversal civilization</li><li><strong>Universal equal infinite law</strong>: basic infinite power is inherent in all; the easygoing retain a guarantee, strivers can superimpose higher; infinite origin erases predatory motivation, predatory involution loses meaning from the root</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Soul-beast extinction is the bill written into the Dou world&#39;s setting. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s verdict: as long as the law that &quot;leveling = killing&quot; is not removed, extinction is not a crisis, but a settlement. What Path D aims to do is precisely cancel this account at the root.</p><p>In the final analysis, Dou Continent · soul-beast extinction crisis · ecological disaster of predatory cultivation described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./392_模块2-斗罗-异族处境-魂兽被定义为资源的悲剧.html">Entry 392 · Foreign-Race Situation</a> · <a href="./384_模块2-斗罗-阿赖耶监管方案-杜绝魂兽灭绝的制度设计.html">Entry 384 · Alaya Supervision Plan</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/46-环境保护法.html">46-Environmental Protection Law</a></li></ul>',29)])])}const m=t(a,[["render",s]]);export{g as __pageData,m as default};
